schema: "0.4"
id: sem-facts-ux-design
type: image
quality: high
product_targets:
  - semtext.dev
tags:
  - semtext
  - sem-facts
  - ux-design
  - reference

prompt:
  text: |
    UX design sheet for the SemText `<sem-facts>` element — a collection of
    fact/claim pairs whose `view-as` selects the recall interaction (list =
    read, flashcards = self-test, quiz = scored recall). Show one example
    reading page per mode, stacked vertically, rendered in the
    minimal-tech-light theme on a dark slate canvas (bg #0f172a, surface
    #1e293b, fg #e2e8f0, muted #94a3b8, accent #60a5fa). Each page sits in
    a browser-chrome frame with a small mono uppercase caption. A fact is a
    bordered card (12px radius, hairline #334155 border, 16px inner
    padding): the statement in the normal foreground at 600 weight, the
    conclusion below it in the muted color. Explicit wrong candidates
    (`incorrect-statement` children) are NEVER drawn as card prose — they
    only ever appear as quiz option buttons.

    Page 1 — caption "LIST (default)". Three fact cards stacked with a
    12px gap, all fully readable in document order, NO interactive chrome
    anywhere on the page — no arrows, no meter, no option buttons. The
    cards read: "JWTs rotate per session" → "Short-lived access tokens;
    the refresh grant issues a new pair."; "Access tokens expire after 15
    minutes" → "The client mints a new pair from the refresh grant; the
    user never re-signs-in mid-session."; "Client secrets never reach the
    browser" → "The confidential client holds the secret server-side; the
    browser only ever sees tokens."

    Page 2 — caption "FLASHCARDS". A deck: a chrome strip with a left
    arrow button, a centered text meter reading "1/3", and a right arrow
    button at the far edges. Below it exactly ONE card: the front,
    statement only, reading "JWTs rotate per session" — the conclusion is
    NOT visible. In the card's lower-right corner a small muted uppercase
    hint reads "CLICK OR PRESS ENTER TO REVEAL". Beside/below, one inset of
    the SAME card flipped: the conclusion revealed, "Short-lived access
    tokens; the refresh grant issues a new pair.", with a 2px accent
    (#60a5fa) focus outline drawn around the card to show keyboard focus.

    Page 3 — caption "QUIZ". All three question cards stacked (quiz does
    not hide non-current cards; the meter tracks position and score). Each
    card: statement as the prompt, conclusion NOT shown in the card body,
    and under it a stack of answer buttons (left-aligned text, 8px radius,
    hairline border, equal width) mixing the wrong candidates and sibling
    conclusions with the one true conclusion. The first card shows the
    answered state: the correct button — "Short-lived access tokens; the
    refresh grant issues a new pair." — with a soft green border (#86efac),
    the wrong buttons muted, and the chrome meter reading "1/3 · score
    1/1". The lower cards keep their buttons unselected.

    Typography: clean system sans (Inter-like), 15–16px body, 1.5 line
    height, generous margins. Restrained: one accent, one muted tone,
    green reserved for the correct pick. No extra chrome beyond the
    flashcards deck strip and the option buttons.
  negative: >
    a fact card drawn as a button or link; statement or conclusion tinted,
    occluded, blurred or barred; the conclusion visible on a flashcard
    front or inside a quiz card body; wrong candidates rendered as inline
    prose in a card body instead of answer buttons; more than one card
    visible on the flashcards page; an arrow strip on the quiz page;
    chrome (arrows, meter) on the list page; neon glow; light background;
    watermark; lorem ipsum.
  style: >
    Flat UI spec sheet, minimal-tech aesthetic, restrained single-accent
    palette, crisp 12px card radius, hairline #334155 borders, generous
    negative space. Looks like a panel from a design-system guide.

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-facts/sem-facts-list-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-facts/sem-facts-primary-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-facts/sem-facts-quiz-render-the-confidential-client-hold-1280.png
    role: reference

output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1280
    height: 1280
    aspect_ratio: "1:1"
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-facts-ux-design.png

requirements:
  modes:
    - id: list
      label: "LIST (default)"
      must_show:
        - three bordered fact cards, each with its statement (600 weight)
          and its conclusion (muted) fully readable
        - no interactive chrome at all on the page
      must_never:
        - draw a fact card as a button or add arrows / meter / options
        - occlude or tint the statement or conclusion
        - render incorrect-statement content as card prose
    - id: flashcards
      label: "FLASHCARDS"
      must_show:
        - the deck strip — left arrow, centered "1/3" meter, right arrow
        - exactly one card visible, front = statement only, with the
          muted "CLICK OR PRESS ENTER TO REVEAL" hint
        - an inset showing the flipped card with the conclusion revealed
          and a 2px accent focus outline
      must_never:
        - show the conclusion on the card front
        - show more than one card at once on this page
        - render the statement as an option button
    - id: quiz
      label: "QUIZ"
      must_show:
        - all three question cards stacked, each with answer buttons
        - the correct option of the answered card with a soft green
          border and the meter reading "1/3 · score 1/1"
        - wrong buttons muted after answering
      must_never:
        - show a conclusion in a card body outside the answer buttons
        - render wrong candidates as inline card prose
        - pre-select answers on the unanswered cards

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    fact-card-is-prose:
      weight: 0.35
      description: >
        Every fact reads as content, not as a control: border + surface +
        padding only; statement in normal foreground, conclusion muted.
      fail_signals:
        - button fills or outlines on a card body
        - tinted, occluded or blurred statement or conclusion
    modes-are-distinct:
      weight: 0.35
      description: >
        List has no chrome; flashcards shows exactly one card plus a flip
        inset; quiz stacks all questions with answer buttons and one
        answered state.
      fail_signals:
        - arrows or meter on the list page
        - the conclusion shown on a flashcard front or a quiz card body
        - quiz cards hidden instead of stacked
    deck-chrome:
      weight: 0.2
      description: >
        The flashcards page carries the left arrow / meter / right arrow
        strip with the meter reading "1/3"; the quiz page keeps only the
        meter, reading "1/3 · score 1/1" over the stacked cards.
      fail_signals:
        - chrome present on the list page
        - an arrow strip on the quiz page
        - meter text missing or wrong
    theme-fidelity:
      weight: 0.1
      description: >
        Dark minimal-tech palette (#0f172a bg, #60a5fa accent, green
        #86efac for the correct pick only), hairline borders, mono
        uppercase captions, exactly three labeled pages.
      fail_signals:
        - light background or multiple accent hues
        - more or fewer than three labeled pages
  reject_if:
    - the conclusion is visible on a flashcard front or a quiz card body
    - wrong candidates appear as inline card prose instead of buttons
    - a fact card is drawn as a clickable button across its whole area
    - the list page carries any interactive chrome
